---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, professionalServiceSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';

const title = 'Fractional CTO Services | Curavest';
const description =
  'Curavest – Fractional CTO Services provide part-time, embedded technology and process leadership for UK operational businesses.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Services', path: '/services/' },
  { name: 'Fractional CTO Services', path: '/services/fractional-cto/' },
];

const included = [
  'Operational and technology diagnosis.',
  'Process mapping and redesign.',
  'Technology strategy for growing businesses.',
  'Prioritisation of technology investment.',
  'Automation planning and implementation.',
  'AI use-case assessment and practical integration.',
  'Systems selection and integration.',
  'Management information and reporting.',
  'Oversight of external technology suppliers.',
  'Delivery planning and change management.',
  'Training and handover to internal teams.',
  'Board-level advice on technology and operational risk.',
];

const notStartingPoints = [
  'A preselected platform.',
  'A generic transformation framework.',
  'A requirement to introduce AI.',
  'A recommendation to replace systems that are working.',
  'A report that leaves implementation to an already overstretched team.',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/services/fractional-cto/"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs), professionalServiceSchema()]}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Curavest – Fractional CTO Services"
    title="A CTO for the operational problems behind the technology"
    lede="A fractional CTO gives an owner or board access to senior technology and process judgement without committing to a full-time technology leadership hire."
    breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  >
    <p class="lede hero-extra">
      Within Curavest, this is one of several complementary services focused on helping operational businesses
      improve performance and make better technology decisions.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ol class="overview-list">
        <li class="overview-item">
          <p class="overview-index">01</p>
          <div class="overview-copy">
            <h2>Diagnose where the business is losing performance</h2>
            <p class="lede">
              The starting point may be a slow quoting process, inconsistent production, poor visibility,
              duplicated administration or a team that has reached its limit.
            </p>
            <p>We trace the process from beginning to end to find:</p>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Where work waits.</li>
              <li>Where information is lost.</li>
              <li>Where responsibility becomes unclear.</li>
              <li>Where people compensate for a poor process manually.</li>
              <li>Where a system is creating friction.</li>
              <li>Where the stated problem is only a symptom.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The outcome is a clear view of the constraint and the options for dealing with it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="overview-item">
          <p class="overview-index">02</p>
          <div class="overview-copy">
            <h2>Redesign the process</h2>
            <p class="lede">The right fix may be operational rather than technical.</p>
            <p>
              A quote turnaround once taking two to three hours was reduced to an average of fifteen minutes by
              addressing two issues: requests were unmanaged in a shared inbox, and ownership was divided
              between several people.
            </p>
            <p>
              A tool then automated most of the quote. But the tool alone was not the solution. Assigning one
              person responsibility for the process from beginning to end was just as important.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="overview-item">
          <p class="overview-index">03</p>
          <div class="overview-copy">
            <h2>Decide whether technology belongs in the answer</h2>
            <p class="lede">Technology is considered in the context of the process it is meant to improve.</p>
            <p>That can include:</p>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Automating repetitive work.</li>
              <li>Improving the flow of information.</li>
              <li>Connecting systems that currently operate separately.</li>
              <li>Creating more reliable management reporting.</li>
              <li>Using AI to review, classify or surface useful information.</li>
              <li>Building a practical solution from several existing systems.</li>
              <li>Selecting and implementing software where a new system is genuinely justified.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              It can also mean deciding not to automate something because the cost, risk or complexity is
              greater than the likely benefit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="overview-item">
          <p class="overview-index">04</p>
          <div class="overview-copy">
            <h2>Oversee delivery instead of handing over a report</h2>
            <p class="lede">Recommendations do not improve a business. Changes that people can use do.</p>
            <p>
              We stay involved while the fix is tested, adjusted and introduced into everyday work. The aim is
              to make the change understandable, measurable and owned by the people who will continue running
              it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-panel">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="scope-grid">
        <div class="scope-col">
          <p class="eyebrow">What is included</p>
          <h2>Fractional CTO support can include</h2>
          <ul class="scope-list scope-list-yes">
            {
              included.map((item) => (
                <li>
                  <Icon name="prove" class="scope-icon" />
                  <span>{item}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="lede scope-note">
            The precise work depends on the constraint. The service is shaped around the business rather than
            a fixed package.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-col">
          <p class="eyebrow">What is not included</p>
          <h2>This is not technology for its own sake</h2>
          <p class="lede">Curavest does not sell software as the solution to every problem.</p>
          <p class="scope-lead-in">The work does not begin with:</p>
          <ul class="scope-list scope-list-no">
            {
              notStartingPoints.map((item) => (
                <li>
                  <span class="scope-dash" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span>{item}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="lede scope-note">
            If the real issue is ownership, communication, layout, workflow or decision-making, that is where
            the work should begin.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container relationship-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Part of a broader set of capabilities</p>
        <h2>Relationship to other Curavest services</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="relationship-copy">
        <p class="lede">
          The fractional CTO service sits alongside other Curavest offerings focused on operational
          improvement and practical technology use.
        </p>
        <p>Depending on your situation, we may recommend:</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>The fractional CTO service as the primary engagement.</li>
          <li>A more targeted project under another Curavest service.</li>
          <li>A combination of both.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We can explore this in an initial conversation.</p>
        <a href="/services/" class="text-link relationship-cta">Explore all Curavest services →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    eyebrow="Talk before you buy"
    title="Talk through the problem before deciding what to buy"
    lede="If a process is holding back growth, start with the process — not a software shortlist."
    ctaLabel="Start a conversation about Fractional CTO Services"
    ctaHref="/start-a-conversation/"
    tone="petrol"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-extra {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .overview-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .overview-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .overview-item:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .overview-index {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-copper);
  }

  .overview-copy {
    max-width: 62ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .overview-copy .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .overview-copy p {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .check-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .check-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .check-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--color-petrol);
  }

  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .scope-col h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .scope-lead-in {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-on-panel-muted);
  }

  .scope-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .scope-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .scope-list-yes li {
    color: var(--color-on-panel);
  }

  :global(.scope-icon) {
    width: 1.1rem;
    height: 1.1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    color: var(--color-petrol-bright);
  }

  .scope-dash {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 0.85rem;
    height: 1.5px;
    background: var(--color-on-panel-muted);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .scope-list-no li {
    color: var(--color-on-panel-muted);
  }

  .scope-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .relationship-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }

  .relationship-grid h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .relationship-copy {
    max-width: 56ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .relationship-copy p {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .relationship-cta {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 63.9375rem) {
    .overview-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }

    .scope-grid,
    .relationship-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
